  "diagnosis": [
    "The old adapter eagerly parsed and cached HTML plus both paragraph views even when only body strings were consumed. On the 526-case uncached render workload this was about 66 times PHP cost.",
    "Single-page, no-TOC rendering now defers native analysis until paragraph access, memoizes it and keeps the original TOC scope. Explicit splitMany batches remain eager.",
    "Rust paragraph extraction reuses the already parsed DOM when inputs match, avoids parsing identical paragraph views twice, and retains validation without serializing unused headings.",
    "The minifier previously copied the whole document for every protected block. Independent blocks now use node placeholders and one restoration pass. Overlapping, nested and colliding replacements retain the sequential algorithm.",
    "XML-invalid controls explain the nine historical minifier mismatches. Ordinary text/attributes now follow libxml while raw script/style text retains controls.",
    "In the 32-page profile, page rendering consumes about 79 percent of saveAsStatic time. There are 2915 cached Markdown calls taking about 0.05 seconds, no paragraph requests, and negligible native reset time. Accelerating Markdown or IPC cannot remove this measured template-rendering cost."
  ],
